​Layout: 12 micro-calibrated De Laval nozzles spaced symmetrically around the 360-degree hull perimeter.
​Pressure Source: Powered by twin 600-liter Composite Overwrapped Pressure Vessels (COPVs) storing ambient or nitrogen-blend gas at 10,000 PSI.
​Function: Fires high-velocity air pulses (moving up to 1,200–1,500 mph) to brake, stabilize, or pivot the ship instantly in zero-atmosphere environments without expending main thruster fuel.
​Space Radiation Shielding Matrix:
